# What pim-cua-bridge never receives, inside each of its `reverse_proxy` blocks: the site's Basic
# login, cookies, headers that claim where a request came from or which page sent it, and the
# relay headers spacesd would trust (the bridge trusts and logs none of them, and passes on only
# a viewer's ticket). The bridge's answers get no CORS headers.
header_up -Authorization
header_up -Cookie
header_up -Proxy-Authorization
header_up -Forwarded
header_up -X-Forwarded-For
header_up -X-Forwarded-Proto
header_up -X-Forwarded-Host
header_up -X-Forwarded-Port
header_up -X-Forwarded-Prefix
header_up -X-Real-IP
header_up -X-Client-IP
header_up -CF-Connecting-IP
header_up -True-Client-IP
header_up -Origin
header_up -Referer
header_up -X-Cua-Principal-Bin
header_up -X-Cua-Relay-Assertion
header_up -X-Cua-Relay-Authorization
header_up -X-Cua-Mesh-Session
header_up -X-Cua-Host-Caller
header_up -X-Cua-Device-Session
header_up -X-Cua-Agent-Session
header_down -Access-Control-Allow-Origin
header_down -Access-Control-Expose-Headers
header_down -Access-Control-Allow-Credentials
